WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.873
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Newspaper Class, level three.

2
00:00:06.173 --> 00:00:09.687
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.987 --> 00:00:16.052
Unit one: Government Systems. Today you will state governance requirements with the mandative subjunctive.

4
00:00:16.352 --> 00:00:19.144
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:23.623
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.483 --> 00:00:25.566
Democracy.

7
00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:30.674
Democracy means a system in which citizens choose their leaders by voting.

8
00:00:31.283 --> 00:00:34.560
A democracy depends on free and fair elections.

9
00:00:35.150 --> 00:00:38.081
Your turn. Say: Democracy.

10
00:00:40.933 --> 00:00:41.888
Democracy.

11
00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:43.918
Constitution.

12
00:00:44.917 --> 00:00:49.018
Constitution means the basic written rules by which a country is governed.

13
00:00:49.617 --> 00:00:52.754
The constitution protects every citizen's rights.

14
00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:56.420
Your turn. Say: Constitution.

15
00:00:59.267 --> 00:01:00.430
Constitution.

16
00:01:01.183 --> 00:01:02.301
Legislature.

17
00:01:03.317 --> 00:01:06.872
Legislature means the group of people who make the laws of a country.

18
00:01:07.483 --> 00:01:10.226
The legislature passed the new education bill.

19
00:01:10.817 --> 00:01:13.457
Your turn. Say: Legislature.

20
00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:17.533
Legislature.

21
00:01:18.283 --> 00:01:19.714
Executive branch.

22
00:01:20.717 --> 00:01:24.504
Executive branch means the part of government that carries out the laws.

23
00:01:25.117 --> 00:01:27.615
The executive branch is led by the president.

24
00:01:28.217 --> 00:01:31.450
Your turn. Say: Executive branch.

25
00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:35.858
Executive branch.

26
00:01:36.617 --> 00:01:37.699
Judiciary.

27
00:01:38.683 --> 00:01:41.763
Judiciary means the courts and judges that interpret the law.

28
00:01:42.350 --> 00:01:46.126
An independent judiciary protects citizens from abuse.

29
00:01:46.717 --> 00:01:49.555
Your turn. Say: Judiciary.

30
00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:53.366
Judiciary.

31
00:01:54.117 --> 00:01:56.023
Separation of powers.

32
00:01:57.017 --> 00:02:01.640
Separation of powers means the division of government into branches that limit each other.

33
00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:05.666
The separation of powers prevents one group from ruling alone.

34
00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:09.820
Your turn. Say: Separation of powers.

35
00:02:12.667 --> 00:02:14.376
Separation of powers.

36
00:02:15.117 --> 00:02:16.373
Federal system.

37
00:02:17.383 --> 00:02:22.413
Federal system means a system that shares power between national and regional governments.

38
00:02:23.017 --> 00:02:26.061
In a federal system, each state has its own laws.

39
00:02:26.650 --> 00:02:29.744
Your turn. Say: Federal system.

40
00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:33.729
Federal system.

41
00:02:34.483 --> 00:02:35.426
Sovereignty.

42
00:02:36.417 --> 00:02:39.554
Sovereignty means the power of a country to govern itself.

43
00:02:40.150 --> 00:02:42.974
Citizens believe sovereignty belongs to the people.

44
00:02:43.583 --> 00:02:46.352
Your turn. Say: Sovereignty.

45
00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:50.282
Sovereignty.

46
00:02:51.067 --> 00:02:54.636
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:55.483 --> 00:03:03.198
Visal, a constitution says 'It is essential that the executive branch be accountable to the legislature.' Why is 'be' used and not 'is'?

48
00:03:04.283 --> 00:03:17.373
That is the mandative subjunctive. After words like essential, vital, demand and insist, we use the base verb for all subjects: that the judiciary remain independent.

49
00:03:18.483 --> 00:03:20.460
So there is no -s for he or she?

50
00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:31.577
Correct. We say 'The law requires that the president submit a budget', not 'submits'. The negative is 'that the legislature not delay the vote'.

51
00:03:32.683 --> 00:03:33.812
Is it formal?

52
00:03:34.917 --> 00:03:43.746
Yes, it is typical of constitutions and policy reports. In a democracy, citizens may insist that sovereignty rest with the people.

53
00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:46.551
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:47.417 --> 00:03:52.504
Grammar focus: Mandative subjunctive: It is essential that plus base verb.

55
00:03:52.804 --> 00:03:53.933
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:54.617 --> 00:03:58.509
It is essential that the executive branch be accountable to the legislature.

57
00:03:59.417 --> 00:04:03.773
The constitution demands that the judiciary remain independent of politicians.

58
00:04:04.683 --> 00:04:07.507
Citizens insist that sovereignty rest with the people.

59
00:04:08.467 --> 00:04:17.191
After essential, vital, demand, insist or require + that, use the base verb for every subject (he be, she submit). Negative: that he not delay.

60
00:04:17.950 --> 00:04:21.845
Be careful! Don't say: I demand that he apologises.

61
00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:26.345
Say: I demand that he apologise.

62
00:04:26.645 --> 00:04:29.608
After demand + that, use the base verb.

63
00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:33.482
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:34.267 --> 00:04:35.721
How Power Is Shared.

65
00:04:36.021 --> 00:04:39.843
A democracy depends on rules that no ruler can change alone.

66
00:04:40.833 --> 00:04:49.102
Most constitutions require that the legislature pass laws, that the executive branch carry them out, and that the judiciary remain independent.

67
00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:54.654
This separation of powers means that no single group can control the whole system.

68
00:04:55.667 --> 00:05:01.474
In a federal system, it is also vital that authority be divided between national and regional governments.

69
00:05:02.467 --> 00:05:06.068
Whatever the structure, sovereignty must ultimately belong to the people.

70
00:05:07.167 --> 00:05:11.110
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:14.414
It is essential that the president blank the law.

72
00:05:14.714 --> 00:05:18.367
A, obeys. B, obey. C, will obeying.

73
00:05:21.933 --> 00:05:23.898
The answer is B: obey.

74
00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:28.118
The power of a state to govern itself is called blank.

75
00:05:28.418 --> 00:05:32.570
A, sovereignty. B, a ballot. C, a treaty.

76
00:05:36.133 --> 00:05:38.040
The answer is A: sovereignty.

77
00:05:39.183 --> 00:05:42.007
The branch that interprets laws in court is the blank.

78
00:05:42.307 --> 00:05:46.901
A, legislature. B, executive branch. C, judiciary.

79
00:05:50.467 --> 00:05:52.304
The answer is C: judiciary.

80
00:05:53.450 --> 00:05:55.055
Choose the correct sentence.

81
00:05:55.355 --> 00:06:02.143
A, I demand that he apologises.. B, I demand that he apologise.. C, I demand that he to apologise..

82
00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:08.733
The answer is B: I demand that he apologise..

83
00:06:09.883 --> 00:06:12.754
According to the reading, no single group should control…

84
00:06:13.054 --> 00:06:18.460
A, the whole system. B, the constitution only. C, every court.

85
00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:24.835
The answer is A: the whole system.

86
00:06:26.033 --> 00:06:29.498
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:06:30.350 --> 00:06:33.870
Why is the separation of powers important in a government system?

88
00:06:42.683 --> 00:06:44.160
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:44.460 --> 00:07:10.347
The separation of powers matters because it stops any one person or group from holding all the power. When the legislature makes laws, the executive branch carries them out and the judiciary checks them, each branch can limit the others. This protects citizens from abuse, keeps officials accountable and makes it harder for a government to ignore the constitution.

90
00:07:10.647 --> 00:07:12.170
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:07:13.083 --> 00:07:19.300
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and mandative subjunctive: it is essential that plus base verb.

92
00:07:19.600 --> 00:07:24.992
Today's value is civic awareness. Know your rights, and use them to build a fairer society.

93
00:07:25.292 --> 00:07:27.828
See you in Unit two. Goodbye!

94
00:07:28.128 --> 00:07:30.665
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

